<BODY STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif">



<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: right"><B>Exhibit 99.1</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B>CORRECTION: Nano Labs Announces Results of Annual
General Meeting of Shareholders</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">HANGZHOU, China, Oct. 25, 2024 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- In the news release
&ldquo;Nano Labs Announces Results of Extraordinary General Meeting of Shareholders,&rdquo; issued October 23, 2024 by Nano Labs Ltd over
GlobeNewswire, we are advised by the company that the final paragraph should be &ldquo;The Share Consolidation will be effective from
5 P.M. on November 3, 2024, Eastern time. The expected market effective date of the Share Consolidation is November 4, 2024 (as of the
opening of business).&rdquo; The complete, corrected release follows:</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">Nano Labs Ltd (Nasdaq: NA) (&ldquo;we,&rdquo; the &ldquo;Company&rdquo;
or &ldquo;Nano Labs&rdquo;), a leading fabless integrated circuit design company and product solution provider in China, today announced
the results of the Company&rsquo;s Annual General Meeting (&ldquo;AGM&rdquo;) held at 10 A.M. on October 23, 2024, Beijing time (10 P.M.,
October 22, 2024, U.S. Eastern time). The proposals submitted for shareholder approval at the AGM have been approved. Specifically, the
shareholders have passed the following resolutions:</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<TABLE CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; width: 100%"><TR STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: justify">
<TD STYLE="width: 0.25in"></TD><TD STYLE="width: 0.25in; text-align: left">(1)</TD><TD STYLE="text-align: left">to effect a share consolidation of every ten shares with
a par value of US$0.0002 each in the Company&rsquo;s issued and unissued share capital into one share with a par value of US$0.002 (the
&ldquo;Share Consolidation&rdquo;), so that immediately following the Share Consolidation and the share re-designation, the authorized
share capital of the Company shall be US$50,000 divided into 25,000,000 ordinary shares of par value of US$0.002 each, comprising (i)
12,141,093 Class A ordinary shares of par value of US$0.002 each, (ii) 2,858,908 Class B ordinary shares of par value of US$0.002 each,
and (iii) 9,999,999 shares of a par value of US$0.002 each of such class or classes (however designated) as the board of directors of
the Company may determine in accordance with the Company&rsquo;s New M&amp;A (as defined below).</TD>
</TR></TABLE>

<P STYLE="text-align: left; font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 74.5pt">&nbsp;</P>

<TABLE CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; width: 100%"><TR STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: justify">
<TD STYLE="text-align: left; width: 0.25in"></TD><TD STYLE="width: 0.25in; text-align: left">(2)</TD><TD STYLE="text-align: left">to amend the Company&rsquo;s memorandum and articles of association
currently in effect by the adoption of a new memorandum and articles of association to reflect the Share Consolidation (after the amendment,
the &ldquo;New M&amp;A&rdquo;); and</TD>
</TR></TABLE>

<P STYLE="text-align: left; font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 74.5pt">&nbsp;</P>

<TABLE CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; width: 100%"><TR STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: justify">
<TD STYLE="text-align: left; width: 0.25in"></TD><TD STYLE="width: 0.25in; text-align: left">(3)</TD><TD STYLE="text-align: left">to approve the appointment of MaloneBailey, LLP as the Company&rsquo;s
independent registered public accounting firm for the fiscal year ending December 31, 2024.</TD>
</TR></TABLE>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">The Share Consolidation will be effective from 5 P.M. on November 3,
2024, Eastern time. The expected market effective date of the Share Consolidation is November 4, 2024 (as of the opening of business).</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"></P>

